      "writtenOn": "2025-02-18T14:58:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t this always the same as `pkvm_get_loaded_hyp_vcpu()`?\n\nIn fact, this function is a little odd as it means we have three different VM identifiers:\n\n (1) `pkvm_get_loaded_hyp_vcpu()` \u003d\u003e the currently loaded vCPU\n (2) The `vm_handle`\n (3) The `kvm_cpu_context`\n \nFurthermore, `kvm_guest_ffa_handler()` actually takes the vCPU as an argument, so we\u0027re probably better off propagating that instead of going via the handle.\n\nIn other words:\n\n```\nstatic struct kvm_ffa_buffers *ffa_get_buffers(struct pkvm_hyp_vcpu *hyp_vcpu)\n{\t\n\tif (!hyp_vcpu)\n\t\treturn \u0026host_buffers;\n\n\treturn \u0026pkvm_hyp_vcpu_to_hyp_vm(hyp_vcpu)-\u003effa_buf;\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "bd778b0a5e3cbf3491074dc75a0fbb76e997b011",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e34bde4_25ba8197",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-24T20:10:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we only need to pass the `vm_handle` and we will have something like this:\n\n```\nstatic struct kvm_ffa_buffers *ffa_get_buffers(u16 vm_handle)\n{    \n    struct pkvm_hyp_vcpu *hyp_vcpu;\n\n    if (vm_handle \u003d\u003d HOST_FFA_ID)\n        return \u0026host_buffers;\n    else\n    \thyp_vcpu \u003d pkvm_get_loaded_hyp_vcpu();\n\n    return \u0026pkvm_hyp_vcpu_to_hyp_vm(hyp_vcpu)-\u003effa_buf;\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "e5fab745_810a493c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "bd778b0a5e3cbf3491074dc75a0fbb76e997b011",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
